{"ld": 211, "paper": "HP134", "session": "132", "title": "Resolve, Directing the Department of Education to Communicate to School Administrative Units and Private Schools the Importance of Adopting Seizure Action Plans (TITLE CHANGE)", "sponsor_id": "h-kuhn-amy", "cosponsor_ids": ["h-graham-anne", "h-meyer-michele", "h-mitchell-christina", "h-murphy-kelly", "s-pierce-teresa"], "committee_code": "EDU", "committee_name": "Education and Cultural Affairs", "summary": {"text": "This bill requires school administrative units and approved private schools to employ at least one individual who has met the training requirements necessary to administer or assist in the self-administration of a seizure rescue medication or a medication prescribed to treat seizure disorder symptoms beginning July 1, 2026. The bill also requires that, beginning in the 2026-2027 school year, all school employees subject to professional development must, for a minimum of one hour of self-directed study, review seizure disorder materials. The bill also requires that a student's parent or guardian must provide written authorization for a seizure medication to be administered at school by a school employee or self-administered at school with a school employee's assistance, a written statement from a physician licensed in this State and the prescribed medication in its unopened, sealed package with the label affixed by the dispensing pharmacy intact. A student's parent or guardian must also collaborate with the school to develop a seizure action plan, which must be kept on file in the office of the school nurse or a school administrator and be distributed to a school employee responsible for the supervision or care of the student. The bill also requires a school administrative unit and approved private school to provide age-appropriate seizure education programming to all students beginning in the 2026-2027 school year.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0134&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "enacted", "status_label": "Finally Passed", "final_disposition": {"label": "Finally Passed", "date": "2025-06-12", "governor_action": "Signed", "governor_action_date": "2025-06-12"}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 211)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0134&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (H-273)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0134&item=2&snum=132", "item": 2}], "amendments": [{"id": "C-A (H-273)", "description": null, "sponsor": null, "status": "Adopted by House & Senate", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0134&item=2&snum=132", "fiscal_note_url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/bills_132nd/fiscalpdfs/FN021102.pdf"}], "committee_actions": [{"date": "2025-04-28", "action": "Work Session Held", "result": null}, {"date": "2025-04-28", "action": "Voted", "result": "OTP-AM"}, {"date": "2025-05-23", "action": "Reported Out", "result": "OTP-AM"}], "committee_reports": [{"label": "Committee report", "recommendation": "Ought to Pass as Amended", "signer_count": null, "signers": [], "signer_ids": []}], "chamber_actions": [{"date": "2025-01-16", "chamber": "House", "action": "Received by the Clerk of the House on January 16, 2025."}, {"date": "2025-01-16", "chamber": "House", "action": "The Bill was REFERRED to the Committee on EDUCATION AND CULTURAL AFFAIRS pursuant to Joint Rule 308.2 and ordered printed pursuant to Joint Rule 401."}, {"date": "2025-03-21", "chamber": "House", "action": "Carried over, in the same posture, to the next special or regular session of the 132nd Legislature, pursuant to Joint Order SP 519."}, {"date": "2025-04-28", "chamber": "J", "action": "Work Session Held"}, {"date": "2025-04-28", "chamber": "J", "action": "Voted: OTP-AM"}, {"date": "2025-05-23", "chamber": "J", "action": "Reported Out: OTP-AM"}, {"